PETEY BENCHMARK HEURISTICS AND GLOSSARY

The Petey Benchmark (name TBD) measures a tool's ability to identify Fields in a PDF, as well as the Field's Type and the other fields in the document it is associated with. The documents are flat PDFs with their metadata removed, so this task must be accomplished strictly with what is printed on the page.

FIELDS
The basic unit of this data set is the Field. A Field is any place on a form that information is supposed to go. It is defined by its location and its Type.

TYPES OF FIELDS
Text
A Text Field contains text, whether it is a two-letter state code or several paragraphs. 

Choice
A Choice Field is a boolean switch, usually a checkbox or a radio button. While these two function differently in practice, they are equivalent in this context.

Printed
A Printed Field is anywhere that the answer is expected to be hand-written: a signature, initials, or a printed name. The date of signing and the signer's title are Text Fields.

GROUPS
Collections of associated Fields are called Groups. Groups of Choice Fields are defined by the question they ask. Groups of Text Fields are specific data types split into multiple Fields: dates, phone numbers, and ID numbers (ie social security or EIN).